  "goodToKnow": "Das Arbeitsrecht is employment law. German law gives employees strong protection: Kündigungsschutz (protection against unfair dismissal) after six months in firms with over ten employees, statutory minimum holidays, sick pay for six weeks, and works councils. Disputes go to the Arbeitsgericht (employment court). Typical contracts start with a Probezeit (probation) of up to six months. It has no plural."
